title: 'frame-system: apply the call filter to the AuthorizeCall origin'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `AuthorizeCall` now checks the runtime call filter against the `Authorized` origin it creates
    for a call whose `#[pallet::authorize]` callback succeeds, and rejects the transaction with
    `InvalidTransaction::Call` if the filter does not allow the call. Such calls already failed at
    dispatch with `CallFiltered`; they are now rejected at transaction validation, before they can
    be included. Runtimes that want an authorized call to stay usable while e.g. safe mode or
    tx-pause is active must allow it in their call filter, as they already had to for dispatch.
crates:
- name: frame-system
  bump: patch
